{"id":"gradient_advection","compound_name":"Graphs::Particles::gradient_advection","source_path":"gradient_advection/gradient_advection.json","category":"Particles","author":"Autodesk","description":"Particle advection by volume gradient","documentation_file":"gradient_advection_docs_ENU.md","documentation":"## Volume Gradient Advection\n\n### `What it Does`\nThis graph advects particles along an aero volume using both the *voxel_velocity* and the density of the *voxel_fog_density* of the aero volume.  This can product some very useful effects, from \"strings\" of particles to embers leaving a fire, depending on your settings.  **Please note:**  this, like all particle and aero systems, is based on a solver and start frames.  Returning to the start frame is required to recalculate changes.\n\n### `How it works`\nAn aero volume is created and sampled via a voxel field, a gradient field is applied and then added to the point_velocity of an advected particle system using a *modifier_influence*.  Several display options are used to alter the ouput display to achieve the look required.\n\n### `Settings`\n***Particle Setup***  \n*density_multiplier* is used on the *voxel_field* before the gradient field is applied.  It multiplies the *voxel_fog_density* result before calculating the gradient.<br /><br />***Modifier Influence***  \nThe relevant settings in this compound are ***rate*** and ***operation***.  This is the compound where the point_velocity is modified to take the gradient field.  The volume and drag influenced connected to this compound drive the particles along the aero velocity.<br /><br />***rate*** controls how quickly the gradient field is applied to the particles; higher numbers equate to faster application.<br /><br />***operation*** controls how the gradient is applied to the *point_velocity*, the options are **replace**, **multiply** and **add**.<br /><br />***Display***<br />Here is where you can choose from many options controlling how your final particles are displayed.\n\n* ***culling_threshold:*** The gradient field is sampled, and its speed calculated.  Any particle whose speed is below the threshold value is deleted.\n\n* ***gradient_high_color, gradient_low_color:*** The particles that remain after culling receive a color interpolated between these values, based on speed.\n\n* ***display_curve:***  adjusts the gradient between *particle_high_color* and *particle_low_color*.\n\n* ***particle_size_curve:***  adjusts the particle radius between fastest and slowest.\n\n* ***particle_size_multiplier:*** A multiplier on the overall size of the particles.","library_dependencies":{"Amino":"2.15.0.9","bif":"2.15.0.9","fields":"2.15.0.9","fluids":"2.15.0.9","geometries":"2.15.0.9","particles":"2.15.0.9","scatter":"2.15.0.9","simulation":"2.15.0.9"},"graph_ports":[{"portName":"particles","portDirection":"output","portType":"Object"}],"terminal_states":[{"name":"Core::Graph::terminal::final","enabled":"false"},{"name":"Core::Graph::terminal::proxy","enabled":"false"},{"name":"Core::Graph::terminal::diagnostic","enabled":"false"}],"counts":{"nodes":57,"connections":83,"values":133,"compounds":4},"node_types":{"Core::Math::multiply":5,"Core::Fields::scalar_field":4,"Core::Graph::pass":4,"Core::Math::length":3,"Simulation::Influence::dissipation_influence":2,"Core::FCurve::evaluate_fcurve":2,"Core::Fields::sample_field":2,"Modeling::Primitive::create_mesh_sphere":1,"noise_on_mesh":1,"Simulation::Aero::aero_solver_settings":1,"Simulation::Aero::simulate_aero":1,"Simulation::Aero::source_air":1,"Simulation::Influence::vorticity_influence":1,"Simulation::Common::vary_source_property":1,"Simulation::Influence::turbulence_influence":1,"Core::Fields::voxel_field":1,"Core::Fields::gradient_field":1,"Simulation::Particles::particle_solver_settings":1,"Simulation::Particles::simulate_particles":1,"Simulation::Particles::source_particles":1,"Simulation::Influence::volume_influence":1,"Simulation::Influence::drag_influence":1,"Sim