e.\n\nThe four influences are used to generate a more interesting shape in the Aero.\n\n***vorticity_influence*** adds curls and rotational movement to the Aero\n\n***turbulence_influence*** adds random motion\n\n***dissipation_influence*** (*voxel_temperature*) fades the temperature of the Aero over time to slow down the lifting.\n\n***dissipation_influence*** (*voxel_fog_density*) fades the density over time to dissipate the Aero."},{"type":"sticky_note","text":"# gradient advection\n\nThis graph adds the **gradient** of the density field to the **velocity** of the particles.\n\nGradient is defined as a vector field where the direction and length of the vector represent the direction and rate of greatest increase of the scalar field at any position."}]}